  "body": "The KV garbage collector stopped the whole cycle on the first group that returned an error, so every group after it was skipped. It now logs the error and moves to the next group.\n\nThe errors this covers are things like a statement timeout on a delete, a transient read error, or an unparseable key. A permanently failing group used to starve every group after it, in every cycle, since groups are scanned in name order.\n\nA cancelled context still stops the cycle, because that means the process is shutting down.\n\nThe SQL backend already behaves this way; only the KV backend stopped early.\n\nTests cover both: a failing group does not stop a later one, and a cancelled context does stop the cycle.\n\nNo config defaults change here.\n",
  "changed_files": 2,
